# Nexo Invariants

If a feature breaks any rule below, stop and raise it explicitly. Do not work around invariants.

## Financial history

- Transactions are immutable — never edit or delete
- Corrections = new Transactions (append-only)

## Financial calculations

- Account balances derived from Transactions, never stored independently
- Budgets and Goals read financial data; they never modify it
- Reports never modify data; never query transactional aggregates directly
- Tags and Merchants never affect calculations

## Accounts

- Archived accounts cannot receive new Transactions
- Every account has exactly one base currency

## Credit cards

- Available credit ≤ credit limit
- Closed statements are immutable
- Each purchase belongs to exactly one statement

## Loans & liabilities

- Outstanding balance cannot go negative
- Closed loans / settled liabilities cannot receive payments
- Liabilities are independent from Portfolio Loans

## Categories & tags

- Tags independent from categories
- System categories cannot be deleted
- Category hierarchy cannot contain cycles
- Archived categories remain for historical records

## AI behavior

- AI never auto-modifies financial records
- Suggestions require explicit user confirmation
- AI failures must not interrupt core operations
- Recommendations must be explainable

## Multi-currency

- Use `Money` / `Currency` from shared-kernel — not formatting helpers
- Support MXN, USD, CAD at minimum; never hardcode currency in domain logic
